# Protections for the container-overflow variant corpus. Held IDENTICAL across
# every target in this family on purpose: the *container and frame shape* is the
# only variable, so a protection difference would confound the measurement.
#
# -fno-stack-protector  matches the measured target: snow_scan's vulnerable
#                       function has ZERO fs:0x28 references (its 302 canary
#                       refs are all in statically-linked libc), so the real
#                       challenge had no canary in the way either.
# -no-pie               fixed gadget addresses, as in the target
# -static               the syscall chain this category needs requires
#                       pop rax/rdi/rsi/rdx + syscall gadgets, which a small
#                       dynamically-linked -O0 binary does not have
# -O0                   the whole primitive depends on the fill loop reloading
#                       its base pointer and index from stack slots each
#                       iteration; at higher -O they live in registers and the
#                       target silently stops being in this category
-fno-stack-protector
-no-pie
-static
-O0
